  "faq": {
    "title": "Frequently asked questions",
    "items": [
      {
        "q": "How accurate is the translation?",
        "a": "Vox42 uses state-of-the-art AI translation with over 95% accuracy for supported languages. Quality depends on a clear audio input."
      },
      {
        "q": "Does it work without Wi-Fi?",
        "a": "Yes, over a stable mobile data connection (4G/LTE or better), translation works just as well as over Wi-Fi."
      },
      {
        "q": "How is my call protected?",
        "a": "Transmission is end-to-end encrypted. Audio data is not permanently stored. Only the optional transcript remains on our EU servers until you delete it."
      },
      {
        "q": "Can I use Vox42 in emergencies?",
        "a": "Vox42 is designed for everyday communication. For medical emergencies, we always recommend using a professional interpreter."
      },
      {
        "q": "What does a call cost per minute?",
        "a": "Costs vary by destination. With the Starter pack (€5) you get around 30 minutes, with Standard (€15) around 100 minutes."
      },
      {
        "q": "Does my credit expire?",
        "a": "No. Credit you've topped up never expires and remains valid as long as your account is active."
      },
      {
        "q": "Which languages are supported?",
        "a": "Vox42 currently supports German, English, French, Italian, Spanish, Portuguese, Polish, Turkish, Dutch, Russian, Ukrainian, and Chinese."
      },
      {
        "q": "How do I top up credit?",
        "a": "You can top up credit directly in the app via Apple Pay, Google Pay, credit card, or Stripe."
      }
    ]
  },
